WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.184 --> 00:00:04.107
- Hello believe nation.

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:05.312
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:06.758
My one word is believe.

00:00:06.758 --> 00:00:08.250
and I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.082
are going to solve all the
major problems of the world.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:12.771
So to help you on your journey today

00:00:12.771 --> 00:00:13.926
we're going to learn seven ways

00:00:13.926 --> 00:00:17.039
to overcome bad situations.

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:18.559
And as always guys as you're listening,

00:00:18.559 --> 00:00:20.715
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:20.715 --> 00:00:22.192
please leave it down the comments below.

00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:23.086
Put quotes around it

00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:25.192
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:26.382
and when you write it down,

00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:29.348
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself too.

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:30.978
Enjoy.

00:00:30.978 --> 00:00:33.728
- [Electronic Voice] Nine, eight.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.836
- So, being an entrepreneur is tough.

00:00:39.836 --> 00:00:40.669
It's one of the hardest things

00:00:40.669 --> 00:00:41.897
you're ever going to do in your life.

00:00:41.897 --> 00:00:43.115
If you think it's going to be easy,

00:00:43.115 --> 00:00:45.108
you're in for a world of pain.

00:00:45.108 --> 00:00:47.140
And so overcoming bad situations

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.428
is going to be part of the game.

00:00:48.428 --> 00:00:49.619
It's something that you're going to deal

00:00:49.619 --> 00:00:50.890
with on a consistent basis.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.261
And so I'm going to share with you

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:55.261
my seven tips on how you can do it.

00:00:58.607 --> 00:01:00.097
Number one is changed your mindset.

00:01:00.097 --> 00:01:01.578
And this is a really important one.

00:01:01.578 --> 00:01:03.517
It's so easy to get sucked in

00:01:03.517 --> 00:01:07.724
and lost in negativity
that you just stay there

00:01:07.724 --> 00:01:09.070
and spiral out of control.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.069
And you as an entrepreneur,
you're the leader.

00:01:11.069 --> 00:01:12.596
There's nobody above you saying hey,

00:01:12.596 --> 00:01:14.651
come on let's do this go, go, go.

00:01:14.651 --> 00:01:15.498
That's on you.

00:01:15.498 --> 00:01:16.909
And especially if you have your team,

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.446
you can't get stuck in a bad place

00:01:18.446 --> 00:01:20.583
because you're going to
bring all your team down

00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:22.412
and they won't be productive either.

00:01:22.412 --> 00:01:24.129
And so start by changing your mindset.

00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:25.865
Look at it as an opportunity to grow,

00:01:25.865 --> 00:01:27.845
to get better, to build stronger.

00:01:27.845 --> 00:01:29.227
Anytime there's something major

00:01:29.227 --> 00:01:30.957
that happens in my business,

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.401
it sucks, but immediately I start to think

00:01:33.401 --> 00:01:34.961
okay how can I make this better?

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.384
How do I solve this problem?

00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:37.822
How do I see this as an opportunity?

00:01:37.822 --> 00:01:39.489
How is this going to
make my business better

00:01:39.489 --> 00:01:41.073
for the long term?

00:01:41.073 --> 00:01:44.620
And as soon as you can
break out of the immediacy

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.446
of the negativity and start
looking at how do I fix this,

00:01:48.446 --> 00:01:51.284
how do I solve this, how do I get better,

00:01:51.284 --> 00:01:52.522
how do I make this stronger?

00:01:52.522 --> 00:01:54.409
As soon as you start asking
those kinds of questions,

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:56.414
it pulls you into positivity

00:01:56.414 --> 00:01:58.720
and it pulls you into the
most important part of all:

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.020
action, fixing the problem

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.855
and actually doing something about it.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.605
Change your mindset.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.645
Tip number two is remember your why.

00:02:09.645 --> 00:02:12.368
This is why it's so important
to have a strong why

00:02:12.368 --> 00:02:13.884
when you're starting your business.

00:02:13.884 --> 00:02:15.295
If you're just starting the business

00:02:15.295 --> 00:02:16.473
because you're trying to make money,

00:02:16.473 --> 00:02:18.575
you're just reaching
some kind of opportunity,

00:02:18.575 --> 00:02:20.160
this is where you're going to quit.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.374
As soon as you start facing
multiple bad situations

00:02:23.374 --> 00:02:25.895
over and over and repeated again,

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:26.728
you're going to quit

00:02:26.728 --> 00:02:28.447
because you thought it was easy money,

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:29.806
you thought it was passive income,

00:02:29.806 --> 00:02:31.810
and so that's why you got into it.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.621
It gets hard; you're going to bail

00:02:33.621 --> 00:02:35.111
and go somewhere else.

00:02:35.111 --> 00:02:36.692
If you have a deep passion for it though,

00:02:36.692 --> 00:02:39.757
you have a strong why as
why you are doing this,

00:02:39.757 --> 00:02:40.936
why it's important.

00:02:40.936 --> 00:02:42.491
This is going to get done.

00:02:42.491 --> 00:02:45.833
Remembering that helps push you through

00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:47.743
the crap that you have to deal with.

00:02:47.743 --> 00:02:49.722
There's a great interview with Steve Jobs

00:02:49.722 --> 00:02:52.511
where he's talking about
you have to kind of be crazy

00:02:52.511 --> 00:02:53.344
as an entrepreneur.

00:02:53.344 --> 00:02:55.137
You have to be crazy
in love with your idea

00:02:55.137 --> 00:02:56.473
because running the business

00:02:56.473 --> 00:02:58.383
and starting it is so hard

00:02:58.383 --> 00:03:00.851
that any sane logical person would quit

00:03:00.851 --> 00:03:03.655
because you're sane, because your normal,

00:03:03.655 --> 00:03:06.000
because your logical, because
it's just way too hard.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.529
Nobody wants to deal with all this crap,

00:03:08.529 --> 00:03:10.232
but the thing that gets you through

00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:11.312
is that strong why,

00:03:11.312 --> 00:03:13.344
that insane passion for what you're doing.

00:03:13.344 --> 00:03:15.288
And so whenever you're down in the hole,

00:03:15.288 --> 00:03:17.395
think back to why you
started this business,

00:03:17.395 --> 00:03:19.305
why it's so important to you.

00:03:19.305 --> 00:03:20.864
You better have a reason other than money,

00:03:20.864 --> 00:03:23.281
otherwise you're in trouble.

00:03:26.009 --> 00:03:27.862
Tip number three is model success.

00:03:27.862 --> 00:03:29.458
Whenever you don't know what to do,

00:03:29.458 --> 00:03:30.792
model a success I find

00:03:30.792 --> 00:03:32.102
is one of the best single strategies

00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:35.089
that you can do to help
you get out of your hole.

00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:36.781
And so find somebody who's been in

00:03:36.781 --> 00:03:38.537
that same situation as you have,

00:03:38.537 --> 00:03:40.264
and how did they overcome it?

00:03:40.264 --> 00:03:41.831
And I find two great things happen

00:03:41.831 --> 00:03:42.834
when you model success

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:45.017
and read their stories
of famous entrepreneurs

00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:46.178
who have come before you.

00:03:46.178 --> 00:03:48.878
One is you get the tactical
things of what to do.

00:03:48.878 --> 00:03:51.096
Like okay Oprah Winfrey went through this

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:53.180
and here's how she came through.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.544
Or Steve Jobs went through this

00:03:54.544 --> 00:03:55.882
and here's how he came through.

00:03:55.882 --> 00:03:57.417
Or Bill Gates had this happen

00:03:57.417 --> 00:03:58.972
and here's how he came through.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.864
And you get the tactics the specific steps

00:04:01.864 --> 00:04:04.508
of what to do that they did.

00:04:04.508 --> 00:04:06.102
Second thing, though that
I think is really important

00:04:06.102 --> 00:04:07.728
is just the motivation.

00:04:07.728 --> 00:04:09.236
Just knowing, at least for me,

00:04:09.236 --> 00:04:11.554
knowing that these people struggled

00:04:11.554 --> 00:04:14.454
and suffered early on in their careers

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.509
makes me feel like I'm not alone.

00:04:16.509 --> 00:04:18.501
Made me feel like if they could do it.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.856
I could do it too.

00:04:19.856 --> 00:04:23.363
And, so I would always
start my day reading

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.842
a story of a famous entrepreneur

00:04:24.842 --> 00:04:25.911
and how they got started.

00:04:25.911 --> 00:04:28.030
Now we use the top ten because it's video

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.624
and I much prefer video,

00:04:29.624 --> 00:04:31.924
but being able to watch somebody's story,

00:04:31.924 --> 00:04:33.727
hear from their advice,

00:04:33.727 --> 00:04:36.028
gave me both the motivation to keep going,

00:04:36.028 --> 00:04:37.874
as well as the tactics on what to do.

00:04:37.874 --> 00:04:39.900
And so whenever you're in the hole,

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.210
at least I found that to be super helpful

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.534
to help me get out.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:44.784
Model success.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.781
- Tip number four is to
focus on a teachable lesson.

00:04:51.781 --> 00:04:53.829
So I had a situation where

00:04:53.829 --> 00:04:56.652
I had a really close
friend of mine betray me

00:04:56.652 --> 00:04:58.859
in the worst way possible.

00:04:58.859 --> 00:05:01.250
She stole something very important to me

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.769
that was really near and dear to my heart.

00:05:04.769 --> 00:05:06.510
And I focused on the negative.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.496
I focused on the bad
situation that happened

00:05:08.496 --> 00:05:11.739
and I carried that
resentment everywhere I went.

00:05:11.739 --> 00:05:14.893
I'm not an angry person at all,

00:05:14.893 --> 00:05:17.442
but I was punching holes through walls.

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:19.166
I was hurting myself.

00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:22.066
I was angry at everything around me

00:05:22.066 --> 00:05:23.529
and I was so resentful

00:05:23.529 --> 00:05:26.113
and angry everywhere I went.

00:05:26.113 --> 00:05:27.751
It affected my relationships.

00:05:27.751 --> 00:05:29.307
It affected my friendships.

00:05:29.307 --> 00:05:32.714
It affected the way I operated at work.

00:05:32.714 --> 00:05:35.210
And I needed to find a solution.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.205
So the solution was to focus
on the teachable lesson.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.416
What can I learn from this?

00:05:41.416 --> 00:05:43.772
I had to learn how to forgive.

00:05:43.772 --> 00:05:45.641
Resentment wouldn't take me anywhere.

00:05:45.641 --> 00:05:47.047
Anger wouldn't take me anywhere,

00:05:47.047 --> 00:05:48.609
but forgiveness can.

00:05:48.609 --> 00:05:51.743
So every single day I worked
on forgiving this person.

00:05:51.743 --> 00:05:53.560
I had to let her go.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.370
Even though I haven't seen her again,

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.870
I no longer hold the need to seek revenge

00:06:00.937 --> 00:06:04.467
to see her suffer because
she made me suffer so badly.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.825
I wish her all the happiness in the world

00:06:06.825 --> 00:06:08.816
and I hope she's doing well.

00:06:08.816 --> 00:06:12.270
So the next time you find
yourself in a bad situation,

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.700
always try to remember
the teachable lesson

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.867
and think to yourself what
can I learn from this?

00:06:21.122 --> 00:06:24.104
- Tip number five is find another way.

00:06:24.104 --> 00:06:27.398
And so this again is why
the why is so important.

00:06:27.398 --> 00:06:28.413
You know, you're down in the hole.

00:06:28.413 --> 00:06:29.348
You're struggling.

00:06:29.348 --> 00:06:30.247
You're sucking.

00:06:30.247 --> 00:06:32.465
You've got no energy left.

00:06:32.465 --> 00:06:36.209
Thinking to yourself what
I have done is not working,

00:06:36.209 --> 00:06:37.916
but there is another way to go.

00:06:37.916 --> 00:06:39.309
This is what I use really effectively

00:06:39.309 --> 00:06:40.360
in my first business.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.176
When I told my partner that I quit,

00:06:42.176 --> 00:06:45.646
when I felt so worthless and useless

00:06:45.646 --> 00:06:46.722
and I had no value,

00:06:46.722 --> 00:06:49.065
I felt like I wasn't bringing
anything to this business

00:06:49.065 --> 00:06:51.065
and I just felt so low I myself,

00:06:51.065 --> 00:06:53.609
I woke up the next day after
telling my partner that I quit

00:06:53.609 --> 00:06:55.251
and I said I have to find another way.

00:06:55.251 --> 00:06:56.674
There has to be another way.

00:06:56.674 --> 00:06:57.736
Someway to solved this.

00:06:57.736 --> 00:06:59.058
There has to be another way.

00:06:59.058 --> 00:07:01.626
It's not that the whole idea sucks.

00:07:01.626 --> 00:07:04.656
Just the way we've been
doing it has sucked

00:07:04.656 --> 00:07:06.087
and there's another path.

00:07:06.087 --> 00:07:07.238
There's another way to stay

00:07:07.238 --> 00:07:08.706
and I've just got to find that.

00:07:08.706 --> 00:07:10.888
And it actually ended up being a blessing

00:07:10.888 --> 00:07:13.119
because good is the enemy of great.

00:07:13.119 --> 00:07:16.101
If what I was doing was kind of working,

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:16.973
I might have just stuck

00:07:16.973 --> 00:07:19.086
with doing what was kind of working,

00:07:19.086 --> 00:07:20.868
but knowing that it wasn't working at all

00:07:20.868 --> 00:07:23.171
meant that I had to find
a totally different path.

00:07:23.171 --> 00:07:25.744
I had to find a totally new innovative way

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:27.664
to market and improve my business.

00:07:27.664 --> 00:07:29.616
And it ended up being my model of success

00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:31.050
by going through partnerships

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.642
by looking at what Bill
Gates did to build Microsoft

00:07:33.642 --> 00:07:35.081
through partnerships and applying that

00:07:35.081 --> 00:07:36.963
to my company and that's
when we started to

00:07:36.963 --> 00:07:38.466
get a lift.

00:07:38.466 --> 00:07:40.791
But just that mindset that

00:07:40.791 --> 00:07:43.676
this isn't total failure
what's happening right now.

00:07:43.676 --> 00:07:45.660
Just the way that I've been doing it,

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:46.974
hasn't been working

00:07:46.974 --> 00:07:49.641
and I need to find another way.

00:07:52.565 --> 00:07:55.063
Tip number six is just go back to work.

00:07:55.063 --> 00:07:56.769
Sometimes the best thing you can do

00:07:56.769 --> 00:07:58.906
is just get back to work

00:07:58.906 --> 00:08:00.641
and start building something.

00:08:00.641 --> 00:08:04.982
When you start taking action
good things start to happen.

00:08:04.982 --> 00:08:06.784
When you are just negative and sad

00:08:06.784 --> 00:08:09.315
and down what ends up happening?

00:08:09.315 --> 00:08:10.201
You don't do anything.

00:08:10.201 --> 00:08:11.364
You sit there and you wallow

00:08:11.364 --> 00:08:12.879
and you stay in your head

00:08:12.879 --> 00:08:15.356
and you get frustrated and you complain.

00:08:15.356 --> 00:08:19.449
And the solution out
sometimes is just do the work.

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:20.801
There was this interview
I was watching recently

00:08:20.801 --> 00:08:21.634
of Joe Rogan.

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:24.442
We're doing a top ten volume two on him.

00:08:24.442 --> 00:08:26.050
He was saying that if he waited

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:27.993
until he was super motivated and excited

00:08:27.993 --> 00:08:29.226
to go out and go work out,

00:08:29.226 --> 00:08:30.913
he would never work out.

00:08:30.913 --> 00:08:32.297
He'd be this fat slob

00:08:32.297 --> 00:08:34.601
because he never feels
motivated to work out.

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:36.975
He forces himself to
just go out and do it.

00:08:36.975 --> 00:08:40.487
And so having a schedule
I find really helps me.

00:08:40.487 --> 00:08:43.561
Knowing what I'm doing
every day really helps me.

00:08:43.561 --> 00:08:45.450
Yes there are some days that I'm inspired

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.656
and motivated and excited.

00:08:46.656 --> 00:08:48.775
I want to do brand new things.

00:08:48.775 --> 00:08:49.608
And when that happens,

00:08:49.608 --> 00:08:51.308
sometimes I'll throw away my schedule

00:08:51.308 --> 00:08:53.096
and just go all in on this new idea

00:08:53.096 --> 00:08:55.487
because gold's going to come out of it.

00:08:55.487 --> 00:08:56.556
But on the days when I wake up

00:08:56.556 --> 00:08:59.057
and I'm not super excited and motivated

00:08:59.057 --> 00:09:00.623
and pumped ready to go you know

00:09:00.623 --> 00:09:01.693
I have my calendars.

00:09:01.693 --> 00:09:02.854
Like this is what I'm going to do today.

00:09:02.854 --> 00:09:03.687
I have a schedule.

00:09:03.687 --> 00:09:04.520
I know what's going to happen.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.750
And if I grind out that work today,

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:06.719
good things are going to happen.

00:09:06.719 --> 00:09:09.269
I'm going to get closer
to achieving my goals.

00:09:09.269 --> 00:09:11.351
And so sometimes the way
out of a bad situation

00:09:11.351 --> 00:09:13.684
is just going back to work.

00:09:17.003 --> 00:09:18.492
And my number seven tip is remember

00:09:18.492 --> 00:09:20.639
that somebody has it worse.

00:09:20.639 --> 00:09:22.643
Both from a global perspective,

00:09:22.643 --> 00:09:24.644
you know the fact that you
are watching this video,

00:09:24.644 --> 00:09:25.876
you have access to the internet,

00:09:25.876 --> 00:09:28.436
you invest in yourself
and personal development

00:09:28.436 --> 00:09:31.107
and watching these you know video content

00:09:31.107 --> 00:09:32.813
to help you get better and improve.

00:09:32.813 --> 00:09:34.549
Just the fact that you are here

00:09:34.549 --> 00:09:37.376
puts you ahead of most
people in the world, right?

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.272
And so the problems that you're facing

00:09:39.272 --> 00:09:40.910
are not actually that big compared to

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.272
what most people in the
world have to deal with.

00:09:43.272 --> 00:09:44.613
That sometimes could help.

00:09:44.613 --> 00:09:45.937
The other thing that
really helps me though

00:09:45.937 --> 00:09:46.840
is also remembering that

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.886
a lot of people that I
look up to the people

00:09:48.886 --> 00:09:52.122
that I aspire to be like
in terms of the impact

00:09:52.122 --> 00:09:53.073
that they're having,

00:09:53.073 --> 00:09:56.330
people have done things amazing things

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:59.849
with fewer resources
than you have right now.

00:09:59.849 --> 00:10:01.937
The people that you look up to people

00:10:01.937 --> 00:10:03.519
who have gone on and done just amazing,

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:06.369
mind-blowing things inside
and outside your industry.

00:10:06.369 --> 00:10:07.319
Your role models.

00:10:07.319 --> 00:10:08.771
Look back to how they started.

00:10:08.771 --> 00:10:12.058
Chances are they started with less

00:10:12.058 --> 00:10:15.915
than what you already have right now.

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:17.625
And so remembering that

00:10:17.625 --> 00:10:19.539
and that they were able to rise up

00:10:19.539 --> 00:10:21.369
and do such amazing things

00:10:21.369 --> 00:10:23.898
and the forced creativity
that had to come from it

00:10:23.898 --> 00:10:25.519
because they didn't
have a lot of resources

00:10:25.519 --> 00:10:27.002
when they were starting their business

00:10:27.002 --> 00:10:29.330
that always turns into motivation for me

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.764
and pulls me through bad times.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.251
So those are my seven tips

00:10:33.251 --> 00:10:35.026
on how to overcome bad situations.

00:10:35.026 --> 00:10:37.128
I'd love to know which
one did you resonate

00:10:37.128 --> 00:10:38.539
the most with and why.

00:10:38.539 --> 00:10:39.944
Is there an eight, nine, 10

00:10:39.944 --> 00:10:40.833
that you want to add to the list

00:10:40.833 --> 00:10:41.980
that maybe I missed?

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.251
leave it down in the comments below.

00:10:43.251 --> 00:10:44.812
I'm super curious to find out.

00:10:44.812 --> 00:10:46.899
I made this video because a Amervin Bonano

00:10:46.899 --> 00:10:47.961
asked me to.

00:10:47.961 --> 00:10:49.244
So if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:10:49.244 --> 00:10:51.395
in a future seven ways video,

00:10:51.395 --> 00:10:52.802
check out the link in the description

00:10:52.802 --> 00:10:55.401
and go and cast your vote.

00:10:55.401 --> 00:10:57.603
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Christi Vlad.

00:10:57.603 --> 00:10:59.185
Christi, thank you so much for picking up

00:10:59.185 --> 00:11:01.249
